cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Edge LLM on FPGAs: four Kria KV260 boards decoding one Llama-3.2-1B stream"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Al-Nafisah
    given-names: Abdullah
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9537-1335"
repository-code: "https://github.com/al-nafisah/llm-kv260"
url: "https://al-nafisah.com/projects/llm-kv260"
abstract: >-
  An int4 weight-streaming matrix-vector engine for the AMD Kria KV260 (Vitis HLS),
  a bit-exact contract for ggml Q4_0 weights and Q8_0 activations, and a
  tensor-parallel runtime that decodes one Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct stream across
  four boards behind an OpenAI-compatible API. Measured numbers are reported in
  docs/buildlog with their raw logs under docs/buildlog/evidence.
keywords:
  - FPGA
  - LLM inference
  - Kria KV260
  - Zynq UltraScale+
  - tensor parallelism
  - Vitis HLS
  - int4 quantization
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
version: 1.0.0
